ggle, inline expanding panels, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, type-aware deliverable launch).\n\n**Stated principles it ships under**\n- **Stdlib-only** Python (single exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals, which degrades gracefully); **all files human-readable/accessible** from any CLI; runs on Python 3.8+.\n\nOne caveat for honesty: this summary is drawn from `CLAUDE.md` and the memory index, not re-verified against the current source â€” but those docs state v2/v3/v4 are built and merged (latest commit work is v4 follow-ups).\n\nWant me to ground any specific claim (e.g., confirm the v4 modules/endpoints actually exist in the code) before you rely on this?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cf9e6d3-f655-4093-ac42-6abab752781b","uuid":"19d2f4f4-4db8-4cb7-bcfc-284e1aa870b5","request_id":"req_011Cc1hX1HKYjXoFrqwi8WrN"}
